<title>USA: General Signal sets stock buyback, unit sale.</title>
<headline>General Signal sets stock buyback, unit sale.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Signal Corp said Monday its directors had approved the repurchase of up to $150 million of the company's common stock. It also said it had agreed to sell its pump business.</p>
<p>&quot;This action was based on the strong financial condition of the company and the attractiveness of buying the shares as a sound way to build shareholder value,&quot; Chief Executive Michael Lockhart said.</p>
<p>The company said it had agreed to sell its pump business to Pentair Inc for about $200 million. Included in the sale will be all businesses and brands of the pump business, including Aurora Pump, Hydromatic, Layne &amp; Bowler, and Fairbanks Morse.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
